– Q.65 Carry TWO mark each.

-- 34 of 69 --

Consider the following program:
int main()
{
f1();
f2(2);
f3();
return(0);
}
int f1()
{
return(1);
}
int f2(int X)
{
f3();
if (X==1)
return f1();
else
return (X*f2(X-1));
}
int f3()
{
return(5);
}
Which one of the following options represents the activation tree corresponding to
the main function?
